# Inline text styles
@scenario tutorial_lesson_33
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[stage clear]
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set tutorial_source scripts/tutorial/33_text_styles.vns]
[set tutorial_excerpt markup]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: See how the same sentence reads when you change where it places the emphasis.
# region markup
ginger: I asked for the {b}blue{/b} notebook, {i}please{/i}.
# endregion
ginger: Move the bold tags to notebook and rerun the line. Keep please italic. Then check that the next line returns to the normal style.
> Replay the line -> start
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Practice exercise -> practice
> Review question -> check
@label return_hub
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[if !tutorial_done_33]
[flag tutorial_done_33]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_7]
[end]

@label practice
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: Remove the closing bold tag in a disposable copy. What should you inspect?
> The image's file name. -> practice_hint
> Where emphasis ends in the rendered line. -> practice_result
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label practice_hint
ginger: Keep opening and closing tags paired so styles have an explicit scope.
[jump practice]
@label practice_result
ginger: Keep opening and closing tags paired so styles have an explicit scope.
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
> Review question -> check
> Try the interactive lab again -> start
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: What changes when you move the bold tags?
> The words that receive emphasis. -> correct
> The speaker's name. -> retry
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show ginger guide confused]
ginger: The speaker ID stays the same. Tags affect the text spans they surround.
[jump check]
@label correct
ginger: The speaker ID stays the same. Tags affect the text spans they surround.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
